      "body": "so do i need to edit helio.py similar to how we changed config and flare_dataset.py ?\n\ni want a code created here between you and me in chat so i can copy it into the notebook that is building off what you just pointed out. id like to get code for a new cell i can run so i can check everything out in 1 cell. ideally, i get:\n\nthe 2 inputs i set in the config file right now, then the time im predicting next to it (ground truth or what'll be forecas), maybe somespace between the inputs and output too.\nid get this with full normal colors (lim = np.percentile(plot_ts[plot_ts != 0], 99)) and a 2nd version where the changes are more visible (ie lim closer to lim = np.percentile(plot_ts[plot_ts != 0], 99)*10 or whatever)\nid get this in just aia131 but also maybe one or two of the other channels to compare (like aia 171). this would be like grouped so channels in 1 row are all the same (diff channel would be in diff rows), we'd end up with like a 2 rows x 3 columns grid where colums are the time differences\nid also like the images that show the pixel differences between the images (between the two inputs, and between the last input and the ground truth). so like a seperate column below the grid i mentioned (it can be centered still, so the formatting of the grid doesn't change)\nbefore or after the images, ideally id also like to:\n\nsee the target i chose (ie the peak or start time image is the ground truth), both timestamp and how close to the actual time the image is, since they're only available in 12 mins intervals.\nand then i also get that actual source location for images so i can double check its doing what i wanted it to",
