              "questions": "[{\"question\":\"Which way did the difference images break?\",\"header\":\"Symptom\",\"multiSelect\":false,\"options\":[{\"label\":\"Saturated blobs\",\"description\":\"The diff panels are solid/near-solid red and blue with little visible structure \u2014 over-saturated. This is what the line 144 fix above addresses (raise diff_gain).\"},{\"label\":\"Washed out / blank\",\"description\":\"The diff panels look almost uniformly white or pale gray, structure invisible. Same fix, but lower diff_gain instead (try 1.5 or 1).\"},{\"label\":\"Layout is wrong\",\"description\":\"Scaling is fine, but the diff panels are misaligned/smaller than the grid above, or overlapping. Likely the colorbar on line 150 shrinking those axes \u2014 different fix needed.\"},{\"label\":\"Wrong frames differenced\",\"description\":\"The diff is comparing the wrong pair of images, or the subtraction labels don't match what's shown.\"}]}]"
